repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/vulonviing/cross-constituency-aggregation-community-notes
abstract: >-
  X's Community Notes shows a crowd-written fact-check only once the crowd
  agrees on it, and how that agreement is measured decides what the public
  sees. Cross-Constituency Aggregation (CCA) sorts readers into groups by how
  they vote and requires a note to earn approval from each group rather than
  from the crowd as a whole, so one camp's enthusiasm cannot outweigh another's
  rejection. This repository holds the full analysis: the 100k-note,
  200k-rater clustering and scoring pipeline, the topic models, the two-stage
  Gemma 4 31B validation of the rescue set, the manuscript, and every committed
  artifact needed to re-derive its results.
keywords:
  - community notes
  - crowdsourced fact-checking
  - social choice
  - spectral clustering
  - content moderation
  - bridging algorithms
